            ("markdown", "## Errors and files\nCatch only errors you expect. `else` runs after a successful `try`; `finally` always runs. `TemporaryDirectory` keeps this small text-file example local and cleans it up automatically. **Try changing this:** use `'not a number'`."),
            ("code", "try:\n    parsed = int('42')\nexcept ValueError:\n    print('Enter a whole number')\nelse:\n    print('Parsed:', parsed)\nfinally:\n    print('Conversion attempt finished')\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom tempfile import TemporaryDirectory\nwith TemporaryDirectory() as folder:\n    note_path = Path(folder) / 'quick_lab_note.txt'\n    note_path.write_text('Practice makes progress.', encoding='utf-8')\n    print(note_path.read_text(encoding='utf-8'))"),
            ("markdown", "## Standard-library modules\n`import` reuses tested code. `math` provides numerical tools, `random.Random(seed)` makes a repeatable local example, and `datetime` represents dates. **Try changing this:** choose another seed."),
            ("code", "import math\nimport random\nfrom datetime import date\nrng = random.Random(7)\nprint(math.sqrt(81), rng.randint(1, 10), date(2024, 1, 1).year)"),
