            ("markdown", "# PyTorch Neural Network\n**Objectives:** Work with CPU tensors, inspect shapes and gradients, define a network, train briefly, run inference, and save a small state dictionary. Run cells in order."),
            ("markdown", "## Tensors, shapes, and device\nA tensor is an array used by PyTorch. This lab explicitly stays on CPU. **Try changing this:** multiply the tensor by three."),
            ("code", "import torch\ntorch.manual_seed(42)\ndevice = torch.device('cpu')\nfeatures = torch.tensor([[0.0], [1.0], [2.0], [3.0]], device=device)\nprint('shape:', features.shape, 'device:', features.device)\nprint('doubled:', features * 2)"),
